this is Rudy Huffman and what you're  seeing is a 30 watt six-round flying  through his brain curve this real  satisfaction I want you to keep this  sight in mind through the rest of the  video and if you do enjoy what you see  remember to like the video and subscribe  to see more  now sniper elite 4 is a game that  rewards precision with gratuitous  violence it asks players to patiently  wait for that perfect moment with the  target in the crosshair aligned then  revel in the satisfaction of making that  organ rupturing bone shattering kill  shot it's hugely satisfying and I enjoy  doing it over and over and over but  after a while I found myself hesitating  to pull the trigger and it was for a  reason that surprised me Sniper Elite  Force tagging system is used to gather  information on your prey and the most  basic it reveals the targets rank  inventory and weapons however tagging  someone can sometimes also display  allies Intel about a soldier this  information could be something about  their personality a relationship with  another soldier or an action from their  past in most video games involve sniping  your hundreds of meters away and this  separation creates a disconnect between  you and your target however sniper elite  force allied Intel bridges the gap and  humanizes the enemy somehow these  tidbits of information make each virtual  soldier feel real and your decision  whether to kill them will spare them  carry more weight from a distance is  easy to see enemies as targets in a  shooting gallery traveling back and  forth along a predetermined path however  for me the Allied in telling you them  with a personality they could be a  simple officer who keeps a photo of  their German Shepherd close to heart or  a cold-blooded killer who murdered a  poor 15 year old boy  obviously the argument exists that  soldiers are just doing their sworn duty  and following their orders just as  protagonist Carl Fairburn is when he  indiscriminately eliminates them but  gang an inside look at the men the game  designates as enemies injects a dose of  morality into the experience and for a  game sold in the back of rupturing  testicles piercing lungs and crushing  skulls with high-velocity bullets that  comes as a welcome surprise discovering  this hidden morality system to sniper  elites gameplay completely changed the  way I played I would spend time tagging  every soldier reading their Intel seeing  how they interacted with other soldiers  and then would slowly untag anyone who I  deemed worthy of keeping their brains  inside of their skulls I became a sort  of judge jury and executioner staying  the executions based on the merits of a  small but impactful piece of Intel I  would choose which lives are taken which  to spare then adapt my path through the  levels so I could avoid the medic that  helps out at enemy soldier while going  out of my way to snuff out the soldier  that opened fire on innocent civilians  instead of mercilessly gunning down  every foe I sought and taking off  objectives I created a new role-playing  wrinkle why punish the bad eggs and the  enemy ranks while sparing the soldiers  who seemed like good people stuck in bad  situations if you're playing Sniper  Elite 4 I recommend revisiting a mission  with this in mind let the Intel you find  make a case of the salvation or  damnation of the people on the other end  of your scope don't give in to the  temptation to kill everyone no matter  how much the game invites you to indulge  your bloodless or how exhilarating it  may be to find that round and see it fly  through a stranger's cerebellum so  remember how I asked you to take note  that shot at the start of the video  looking at the character's history do  you think he deserved it thanks so much  for watching this video about sniper  elites for hidden morality system it  became more than a gory sniper simulator  for me and I would love to hear your  thoughts whether you agree with me or  not I encourage you 